course: dictionary
lesson: 11217
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one fits. Wood can be the hard material that trees are made of. «The cottage was built of wood» tells you it is the material, because you can build with wood. Ask yourself: is the word a thing, or a place?
explain: «There seemed to be no end to this wood, and no beginning, and no way out.» The clues are no end and no way out, so wood here means a small forest, a place you could get lost in. Try your meaning in the sentence: "no end to this forest" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Phrases can also change a word's meaning. «We are not out of the woods yet» has nothing to do with trees. It means we are not safe yet. When you meet a phrase you do not know, look at the whole sentence first, and if you are still stuck, check a dictionary.
fact: Context tells you which meaning of a word fits.
fact: «Wood» means the hard material that trees are made of, used for building, furniture and fires.
fact: «A wood» or «the woods» means a small forest.
fact: «A piece of wood» means a plank, stick or log.
fact: «Not out of the woods yet» means not safe yet.
exercise: «The cottage was built of wood, with a red door.» What does wood mean here? | *The hard material trees are made of | A sunny field of grass | A bird's nest | A small forest
exercise: «Mia got lost in the woods on her way home.» What does woods mean here? | A river bank | A pile of logs | *A small forest | The hard material used for furniture
exercise: «Tom picked up a piece of wood to make a sword.» What is a piece of wood? | A kind of bird | *A plank, stick or log | A small forest | A cup of hot tea
test: «There seemed to be no end to this wood, and no way out.» What does wood mean here? | A bird's nest | The hard material trees are made of | *A small forest | A piece of furniture
test: In science, what does wood do when you put it on water? | It turns to ice | It melts into a liquid | It sinks straight to the bottom | *It floats
exam: Dad says, «Touch wood, we are not out of the woods yet.» What does not out of the woods yet mean? | *Not safe yet | Out of wood for the fire | Lost in a forest | Finished with all the trees
